{
  "adjacency": {
    "attr": "Two graphs are attribute-row-adjacent if they differ in the attribute vector of one node. The node set and all edges are identical.",
    "edge": "Two graphs are edge-adjacent if they differ by one edge (added or removed). The node set and all attributes are identical."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Selection of attributes and of their top-K values is data-dependent when done on the real data and is NOT covered by the guarantee.",
    "The per-measurement degree caps, the public maximum degree Dmax, the histogram grid, the degree bin edges (including the degree bins of the attribute-degree tables and, when set, the choice of attributes they are measured for), the minimum degree of the clustering statistic and the budget shares were chosen by looking at (non-private statistics of) the real graph; this choice is NOT covered by the guarantee. The shipped values and the cap salt are fixed public constants.",
    "The homophily attribute groups measured by attr_edge_pair (homophily_groups, or the single-group homophily_attrs alias) and the hard limit max_homophily_groups on their number were chosen by looking at a non-private ranking of the real graph; this selection is NOT covered by the guarantee. Attributes in no configured group get no edge-pair measurement and are expected to mix at chance level in the synthetic graph.",
    "The node count n is public: it is the same under both adjacency relations.",
    "The guarantee is stated per adjacency (edge-DP and attribute-row-DP separately); nothing is claimed for a simultaneous change of an edge and an attribute row, or for node-DP.",
    "Sensitivities are proved worst-case bounds (not empirical maxima) and are not tight for every measurement; the realised privacy loss can only be smaller than the ledger states.",
    "Post-processing (clamping, rescaling to the public n, symmetrisation, consistency) is free."
  ],
